slug: breathlessness-self-management
title: Breathlessness — Positions, Pacing and Breathing Control
area: Cardiorespiratory
level: Foundation
best: 2nd year onwards
minutes: 11
hook: Breathlessness is frightening, and fear makes it worse. Learn the simple positions, pacing and breathing techniques that patients can use at home to take back control. || Saans ki tangi dara deti hai, aur dar usay barhata hai. Woh saadi positions, pacing aur saans ke tareeqe seekhein jo mareez ghar par istemal karke qaboo wapas pa sakte hain.
goal: By the end, you'll teach pursed-lip breathing, breathing control, recovery positions, pacing and a hand-held fan, set a simple action plan and recognise when breathlessness is an emergency. || End tak aap pursed-lip breathing, breathing control, recovery positions, pacing aur hath ka pankha sikhayenge, saada action plan banayenge aur pehchanenge ke saans ki tangi kab emergency hai.

say: In long-term lung or heart disease, breathlessness often comes with **panic**: the person breathes faster, which makes the breathing harder and the fear worse. The aim of self-management is to **break that cycle** with a few tools: **positions** that ease breathing, **pursed-lip breathing**, **pacing** the day and **a fan** on the face. These do not cure the disease, but they help the person feel in control. || Lambi phephron ya dil ki bimari mein saans ki tangi aksar **ghabrahat** ke saath aati hai: shakhs tez saans leta hai, jis se saans lena mushkil aur dar barh jata hai. Self-management ka maqsad **is chakkar ko torna** hai kuch auzaar se: saans aasan karne wali **positions**, **pursed-lip breathing**, din ki **pacing** aur chehre par **pankha**. Yeh bimari ka ilaj nahi, magar shakhs ko qaboo mein mehsoos karwate hain.
analogy: Think of breathlessness as **a car in a skid**. Slamming the brakes makes it worse. The calm response is to ease off, steer gently and let the car recover. Slow, relaxed breathing out and a supported position are the gentle steering that help the body regain control. || Saans ki tangi ko **phislti hui gaari** samjhein. Achanak brake dabana halat bigarta hai. Pur-sukoon jawab yeh hai ke raftar kam karein, narmi se steer karein aur gaari ko sambhalne dein. Aahista, dheeli saans bahar nikalna aur sahara dene wali position woh narm steering hain jo jism ko qaboo wapas dilati hai.
steps: Teaching self-management || Self-management sikhana
step: Find the triggers :: Ask when breathlessness is worst (stairs, dressing, bathing, anxiety) and what the person fears. Check they have seen the doctor about worsening symptoms. || Triggers dhoondein :: Poochhein saans ki tangi kab sab se zyada hoti hai (seedhiyan, kapray, naha'na, ghabrahat) aur shakhs ko kis cheez ka dar hai. Dekhein ke kya unhon ne barhti alamaat par doctor ko dikhaya.
step: Teach a recovery position :: Leaning forward with the forearms on a table or the knees, shoulders relaxed, or sitting upright against a wall. These positions let the chest muscles work with less effort. || Recovery position sikhayein :: Aage jhuk kar bazu mez ya ghutnon par, kandhe dheelay, ya deewar se tek laga kar seedha baithna. In positions mein seene ke muscles kam mehnat se kaam karte hain.
step: Teach pursed-lip breathing :: Breathe in gently through the nose for two counts, then out slowly through lips as if blowing a candle for four counts. Do not force the breath out. || Pursed-lip breathing sikhayein :: Naak se aahista do ginti tak saans lein, phir hontoon se jaise mombatti phoonk rahe hon chaar ginti tak aahista bahar nikalein. Saans zabardasti bahar na nikalein.
step: Plan the day :: Pace tasks, rest before you are exhausted, breathe out on the effort (for example when standing up or lifting) and use a hand-held fan on the cheeks. Write a simple plan for a bad day. || Din ka plan banayein :: Kaamon ki pacing karein, thakne se pehle aaram karein, mehnat par saans bahar nikalein (maslan uthte ya uthate waqt) aur gaalon par hath ka pankha istemal karein. Kharab din ke liye saada plan likhein.

check: Which breathing pattern is taught for breathlessness? || Saans ki tangi ke liye kaun sa saans ka pattern sikhaya jata hai?
ok: In through the nose, then out slowly through pursed lips, longer than the breath in || Naak se andar, phir pursed hontoon se aahista bahar, andar se lambi || Yes — slow breathing out keeps the airways open and calms the pattern. || Haan — aahista saans bahar nikalna saans ki naliyon ko khula rakhta hai aur pattern ko pur-sukoon karta hai.
no: Fast, deep breaths through the mouth || Tez, gehri saans munh se || That increases breathlessness and fear. || Yeh saans ki tangi aur dar barhata hai.
no: Holding the breath for as long as possible || Jitni der ho sake saans rokna || That makes it worse. || Yeh halat bigarta hai.
compare: Panic breathing or controlled breathing? || Ghabrahat ki saans ya qaboo ki saans?
head: Feature || Khasiyat ;; Panic breathing || Ghabrahat ki saans ;; Controlled breathing || Qaboo ki saans
row: Rate || Raftar ;; Fast and shallow || Tez aur oopar oopar ki ;; Slow and relaxed || Aahista aur dheeli
row: Muscles || Muscles ;; Tense shoulders and neck || Tight kandhe aur gardan ;; Relaxed shoulders, supported arms || Dheelay kandhe, sahara liye bazu
row: Breath out || Saans bahar ;; Short || Chhoti ;; Longer than the breath in, through pursed lips || Andar se lambi, pursed hontoon se
row: Effect || Asar ;; Feels worse and more frightening || Zyada kharab aur dara dene wali ;; Eases effort and fear || Mehnat aur dar kam karti hai
memory: **Lean, lips, slow.** Lean forward with support, breathe out through pursed lips, and slow down. Add a fan on the face and the person usually feels better within minutes. || **Jhukein, hont, aahista.** Sahare ke saath aage jhukein, pursed hontoon se saans bahar nikalein, aur raftar kam karein. Chehre par pankha lagayein to shakhs aam taur par chand minute mein behtar mehsoos karta hai.
mistake: **Telling the patient to "just relax and breathe deeply".** Deep breathing in is not the aim and can make air trapping worse. Teach slow breathing out, a supported position and a clear plan, and explain that breathlessness is uncomfortable but not itself harmful in a stable condition. || **Mareez ko "bas relax karo aur gehri saans lo" kehna.** Gehri saans andar lena maqsad nahi aur air trapping bigaad sakta hai. Aahista saans bahar nikalna, sahare wali position aur saaf plan sikhayein, aur samjhayein ke stable halat mein saans ki tangi takleef deh hai magar khud nuqsandeh nahi.
check: Which position helps a breathless patient? || Saans ki tangi wale mareez ki madad kaun si position karti hai?
ok: Leaning forward with the forearms supported on a table or knees || Aage jhukna, bazu mez ya ghutnon par tike hue || Yes — it supports the shoulders and lets the chest muscles work. || Haan — yeh kandhon ko sahara deti hai aur seene ke muscles ko kaam karne deti hai.
no: Lying flat on the back || Peeth ke bal seedha letna || That often worsens breathlessness. || Yeh aksar saans ki tangi barhata hai.
no: Standing with arms raised || Bazu oopar kar ke khara hona || That tires the shoulders. || Yeh kandhon ko thaka deta hai.
check: When is breathlessness an emergency? || Saans ki tangi emergency kab hoti hai?
ok: Severe breathlessness at rest with blue lips, chest pain, confusion or drowsiness || Aaram mein shadeed saans ki tangi, neelay honth, seene ka dard, uljhan ya neend || Yes — these need urgent medical help. || Haan — in ko foran medical madad chahiye.
no: Mild breathlessness after climbing stairs || Seedhiyan chadhne ke baad halki saans ki tangi || That can be usual for the person. || Yeh shakhs ke liye aam ho sakti hai.
no: Breathlessness that settles with rest and pacing || Aaram aur pacing se thamne wali saans ki tangi || That fits the usual pattern. || Yeh aam pattern se milti hai.
clinic: **Make a one-page plan.** Write the person's three best tools (their position, their breathing and the fan), the signs that mean call the doctor and the signs that mean call the ambulance. Practise them together while the person is calm, not only during an attack. || **Ek safha ka plan banayein.** Shakhs ke teen behtareen auzaar (position, saans aur pankha), woh nishaniyan jin par doctor ko call karna hai aur woh jin par ambulance bulani hai likhein. Inhein shakhs ke pur-sukoon hone par saath practise karein, sirf daure ke dauran nahi.
reveal: Why does breathing out slowly through pursed lips help? || Pursed hontoon se aahista saans bahar nikalna madadgar kyun hai? || It creates a small resistance that keeps the airways open for longer, so less air is trapped in the lungs, and the slow rhythm calms the breathing pattern. Many people also feel less anxious because they have a technique to use. || Yeh ek chhoti rukawat paida karta hai jo saans ki naliyon ko zyada der khula rakhti hai, is liye phephron mein kam hawa phansti hai, aur aahista rhythm saans ka pattern pur-sukoon karta hai. Bohat se log kam ghabrahat bhi mehsoos karte hain kyunke unke paas istemal karne ka tareeqa hota hai.
case: A 66-year-old man with COPD becomes breathless and anxious climbing the stairs. He stops, gasps and says "I cannot breathe". His oxygen level is normal for him and he has no chest pain. || The picture is exertional breathlessness with anxiety, with no emergency signs. || Help him to lean on the rail, teach pursed-lip breathing and a fan, then discuss pacing the stairs. || After practice, he recovers in a minute or two and climbs the stairs by pacing steps with a rest on the landing.
safety: **Call for urgent help** for severe breathlessness at rest, blue lips, chest pain, confusion, drowsiness, fainting, coughing blood or a sudden onset with calf pain. Do not teach self-management as a replacement for medical review when symptoms are getting worse. Follow the doctor's advice on inhalers and oxygen. || **Foran madad bulayein** aaram mein shadeed saans ki tangi, neelay honth, seene ka dard, uljhan, neend, behoshi, khoon ki khansi ya achanak shuruaat pindli ke dard ke saath. Barhti alamaat mein self-management ko medical review ka mutabadil na sikhayein. Inhaler aur oxygen par doctor ka mashwara maanein.
summary: Breathlessness often brings panic that makes it worse; self-management breaks the cycle with positions, pursed-lip breathing, pacing and a fan. || Saans ki tangi aksar ghabrahat laati hai jo usay bigarti hai; self-management positions, pursed-lip breathing, pacing aur pankhe se is chakkar ko torta hai.
summary: Breathe in gently through the nose and out slowly through pursed lips, lean forward with support, and breathe out on effort. || Naak se aahista andar aur pursed hontoon se aahista bahar saans lein, sahare ke saath aage jhukein, aur mehnat par saans bahar nikalein.
summary: Write a simple action plan and teach the signs of an emergency. || Saada action plan likhein aur emergency ki nishaniyan sikhayein.
card: What is pursed-lip breathing? || Pursed-lip breathing kya hai? || Breathing in through the nose and slowly out through pursed lips. || Naak se andar aur pursed hontoon se aahista bahar saans lena.
card: Name a recovery position. || Recovery position ka naam batayein. || Leaning forward with the forearms supported on a table or knees. || Aage jhukna, bazu mez ya ghutnon par tike hue.
card: Why use a hand-held fan? || Hath ka pankha kyun? || Air on the face can reduce the sensation of breathlessness. || Chehre par hawa saans ki tangi ka ehsaas kam kar sakti hai.
card: When is breathlessness an emergency? || Saans ki tangi emergency kab hai? || At rest with blue lips, chest pain, confusion or drowsiness. || Aaram mein neelay honth, seene ka dard, uljhan ya neend ke saath.
deeper: Airway clearance lesson || /learn/airway-clearance-acbt || Clearing secretions safely. || Balgham mehfooz tareeqe se saaf karna.
deeper: Six-minute walk test lesson || /learn/six-minute-walk-test-breathlessness || Measuring effort and breathlessness. || Mehnat aur saans ki tangi naapna.
source: Bausewein C, Booth S, Gysels M, Higginson I. Non-pharmacological interventions for breathlessness in advanced stages of malignant and non-malignant diseases. Cochrane Database Syst Rev 2008;(2):CD005623. || non-pharmacological interventions breathlessness advanced malignant non-malignant Cochrane
source: Spruit MA, Singh SJ, Garvey C, et al. An official American Thoracic Society/European Respiratory Society statement: key concepts and advances in pulmonary rehabilitation. Am J Respir Crit Care Med 2013;188:e13-e64. || ATS ERS statement key concepts advances pulmonary rehabilitation
